# What a consumer gets, and does not.
#
# `.gitignore` decides what is committed; this decides what is PUBLISHED, and
# they are different questions. Everything below is kept in the repository on
# purpose and has no reader on the other side of `pub add xtask`.

# Working notes, not documentation. `doc/research/ci-drift-prior-art.md` is
# 46 KB — larger than the README — and it is the reasoning behind one decision
# rather than anything a consumer of the package reads. The ADRs beside it are
# published deliberately: each is a page, and each answers "why does it refuse
# this?", which is the question a consumer actually arrives with.
doc/research/
